Refulgus Grue.wikitext:
{{NurglePortal}}{{DeathGuardPortal}}
'''Refulgus Grue''' is a [[Death Guard]] [[Plague Champion]].{{Fn|1b}}
[[File:DGHeroes6.png|250px|thumb|right|Refulgus Grue]]

==History==
He has been well blessed by his worship of the [[Chaos God]] [[Nurgle]], which has left Grue with supernatural strength, immunity to pain and being almost impossible to kill.{{Fn|1b}}. In [[M42]], Grue was among the renowned warriors that the [[Necron Overlord]] [[Trazyn the Infinite]] kidnapped and placed in an arena within the Overlord's hidden '''Sanctum''', which is connected to the [[Tomb World]] [[Solemnace]], via [[Reality-Tether]]s. The [[Plague Champion]] then found himself facing the [[Blood Angel]] [[Rafelo]], the [[Ultramarine]] [[Markus Castus]] and the [[Necron]] [[Teknoth]]. They were all brought there to fight for Trazyn's enjoyment, but the Overlord promised the victor would be freed from their imprisonment{{Fn|1a}}. In his fevered mind, Grue knows he is the mightiest warrior to step foot in the Trazyn's arena and the Plague Champion will gladly prove this in Nurgle's name.{{Fn|1b}}. However unbeknownst to Grue and the other warriors, the Overlord has no intention of freeing the arena winner. Instead the victor will have the honor of taking a place of pride within Trazyn's latest exhibit on Solemnace.{{Fn|1a}}   

