Remo.wikitext:
{{InquisitionPortal}}{{ChaosPortal}}
'''Remo''' is the [[Interrogator]] for the [[Radical]] [[Inquisitor]] [[Tjejren]], who turned him into a [[Daemonhost]].{{Fn|1}} 
==History==
[[Tjejren]]'s [[Radicalism]] led him to be hunted in the eastern part of the [[Realm of Ultramar]], during the [[Plague Wars]], by the forces of [[Tetrarch of Ultramar|Tetrarch]] [[Felix (Tetrarch)|Felix]]. The [[Inquisitor]] and his retinue inflicted heavy losses on their attackers, which allowed Tjejren to escape. Remo, however, was captured and Tetrarch Felix planned to destroy the [[Daemonhost]] [[Interrogator]] immediately. [[Lord Commander]] [[Guilliman]] interceded, though, as he truly believed the Interrogator's [[Daemon]] could tell what was occurring on the corrupted [[Ultramar]] world [[Iax]]. It was Guilliman's hope that the answers Remo's Daemon provided him, would prevent Iax from being forever lost to the [[Imperium]]. In order to ensure his questions would be answered, Guilliman had Remo secretly taken from Felix's hold and transferred to his flagship [[Macragge's Honour]]. Once he was there, Remo was placed under the guard of [[Grey Knights Brother-Captain|Brother-Captain]] [[Ionan Grud]] and the [[Concilia Psykana]], until Guilliman was ready to question him.{{Fn|1}} 

When he learned of this, [[Felix (Tetrarch)|Felix]] was furious, as he now knew [[Guilliman]] would try to question Remo's [[Daemon]]. The [[Tetrarch of Ultramar|Tetrarch]] then quickly traveled to the [[Macragge's Honour]] and confronted the [[Lord Commander]] in an attempt to stop him from making a horrible mistake. Felix stated that the [[Interrogator]] was now a creature of both [[Tjejren]] and [[Chaos]] and warned Guilliman that nothing Remo's [[Daemon]] said could be trusted. The Lord Commander's experts in the [[Concilia Psykana]], however, claimed that Remo's soul still clung to his body. Guilliman believed, this was because Remo wanted to perform one last service to the [[Imperium]]. This in turn, the Lord Commander thought, would force the Interrogator's Daemon to truthfully answer his questions. Felix was not convinced, but he relented after Guilliman swore Remo would be killed, after the Lord Commander was finished questioning the Daemon.{{Fn|1}} 

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Dark Imperium: Godblight (Novel)]], Chapter 1

