{{DeathGuardPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is a [[Death Guard]] [[Champion]], who was among its forces that invaded{{Fn|1}} the [[Imperium]] world [[Korvon II]], under the command of the [[Chaos Lord]] [[Felthius]], sometime after the [[Great Rift]]'s creation.{{Fn|2}}  

The world's population was able to send out a distress call, which was answered by an [[Ultramarines]] strike force led by [[Lieutenant (Space Marine)|Lieutenant]] [[Calsius]].  When their [[Strike Cruiser]], the ''[[Honour of Ultramar]]'', neared [[Korvon II]], it was attacked{{Fn|3}} by a [[Chaos Lord|Lord]] [[Felthius]]' warship, ''[[Rotbringer]]''.  The Death Guard soon boarded the ''Honour of Ultramar'' and Repugnus was among them, along with his followers [[Gruhl]] and [[Bubox]]. During the boarding attack, the [[Champion]] was given the task of claiming the skull of one of the Ultramarines' heroes, which served as an inspiring relic for the [[Chapter]].  As battle waged across the ''Honour of Ultramar'', Repugnus and his followers neared the training area where the relic was kept, but they were confronted{{Fn|1}} by a squadron of [[Intercessor]]s. Led by [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] [[Decius (Ultramarines Sergeant)|Decius]], the Intercessors{{Fn|3}}, were the only thing stopping the Champion from achieving his goal.{{Fn|1}}

Repugnus would fail in his task, though, and the Ultramarines repelled the Death Guard from the [[Honour of Ultramar]]. Their battle would continue on [[Korvon II]], however, and Repugnus later defended one of [[Chaos Lord|Lord]] [[Felthius]]' [[Malignant Plaguecaster]]s, as he attempted to open a [[Warp]] portal in the city of '''Mirefurt'''.{{Fn|4}}

