Rinas Dol.wikitext:
{{BloodAngelsPortal}}
'''Rinas Dol''' was a member of the [[Blood Angels]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]], who took part in the [[Horus Heresy]]'s [[Siege of Terra]].{{Fn|1a}}
==History==
He would be among the [[Imperial]] forces that were outside of the [[Imperial Palace]]'s [[Eternity Gate (Imperial)|Eternity Gate]], when it was closed near the end of the [[Siege of Terra|Siege]]. Afterwards, Dol became part of the Imperials that rallied under the command of the [[Imperial Fists]] Commander [[Archamus II]]. This united force fought many battles against the [[Traitor]]s, but during one at the Palace's '''Delphine Viaduct''', they bombarded the [[Traitor]]s and caused them to retreat. This allowed the Imperials to gain new territory near the Viaduct and they secured it, as they waited for the Traitors to return. [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Fafnir Rann]] though, sought to further expand their new territory by securing the ruins of the '''Hasgard Gate'''.{{Fn|1a}} 

It was among the areas struck by the [[Imperials]]' bombardment and with [[Archamus II]]' permission, [[Fafnir Rann|Rann]] led his forces to claim the '''Hasgard Gate'''. He would be joined by the forces of the [[Blood Angel]] [[Zephon (Heresy)|Zephon]] and [[White Scar]] [[Namahi]], who aided the Captain's forces in reaching the area. While the surface of the Hasgard Gate was clear of foes, the [[auspex]] of the White Scars' scouts, had detected several in the bunkers that lay beneath its surface. To clear them out would require close combat work, so Rann chose to send a small force to cleanse the area. The Captain, Zephon and Namahi would each go and also selected two members of their [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]]s to join them. Rinas Dol was among Zephon's Blood Angels forces and was chosen for the task, alongside [[Kystos Gaellon]]{{Fn|1a}}. Though it was a tough fight, the bunkers were successfully cleansed{{Fn|1b}} and afterwards the Gate was secured, as the Legionaries prepared for the Traitors to attack it.{{Fn|1c}}   

