Rothwyr Morvans.wikitext:
{{GreyKnightsPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' was a [[Grey Knights Grand Master|Grand Master]] of the [[Grey Knights]]. He commanded the [[5th Brotherhood (Grey Knights)|5th Brotherhood]] as '''Protector of the [[Sanctum Sanctorum]]'''{{Fn|1}} and acted as ''de facto'' [[Chief Apothecary]].{{Fn|2}}

==History==
Grand Master Morvans was one of the few that spoke with the chapter's ancient [[Grey Knights Dreadnought|Dreadnought]]s, often awakening them for war. In battle, the 5th would often be deployed alongside several Dreadnoughts, as Morvans was aware that if one of these deathless warriors is left too long dormant he might never be roused. It is a cycle of war that the Dreadnoughts are doomed to repeat endlessly, as long as the Chapter has need of their might.{{Fn|1}}

During the [[Season of Blood]], Morvans and the 5th were deployed to [[Armageddon]] to prevent its fall to a massive [[Khornate]] horde under the [[Daemon Primarch]] [[Angron]]. During the campaign, Morvans acted as the key Imperial leader, organizing other warlords such as [[Logan Grimnar]] and [[Helbrecht]] aboard the Grey Knights [[Battle Barge]] ''[[Bright Sword]]''.{{Fn|3b}} In the final stages of the battle he piloted a [[Dreadknight]] and led the assault on the [[Red Angel's Gate]], seeking to seal it and end the [[Chaos]] threat. He engaged Angron personally, suffering grievous injuries but pushing both of them through the [[Warp Portal]] before it was sealed by the Grey Knights. Morvans vanished  while locked in combat with Angron as Armageddon was saved from corruption.{{Fn|3c}}

