Rowd.wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
'''Rowd''' was a [[trooper]] of the [[Imperial Army]], active on [[Calth]] during the [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
Rowd's father was a [[sniper]] in the Army, and Rowd was noted to have inherited his father's skill with a [[long-las]].{{Fn|1}}

Before the Heresy, Rowd was a farmer with a wife and young daughter who worked in the [[Vollard Meadows]]. At one point, Rowd's overseer assaulted Rowd's wife, but Rowd killed him. Now a convicted murderer, he was recruited into the Imperial Army as a [[Penal Legion|penal conscript]] assigned to the [[Numinus regiment]].{{Fn|1}}

Part of the forces mustered on Calth when the [[Word Bearers]] [[Battle of Calth|turned]] on the [[Ultramarines]], Rowd was folded into the guerrilla forces that fought for the [[Imperium]] in the [[Underworld War]].{{Fn|1}}

At one point he was undergoing rad-scrubbing alongside the Ultramarine [[Aeonid Thiel]] when their section of Calth's underground complexes was attacked by a unit of Word Bearers led by the [[Dark Apostle]] [[Kurtha Sedd]]. Together, Thiel and Rowd were able to escape to the surface and survive an assault by the [[Gal Vorbak|Unburdened]] [[Kaeloq]]. They later returned to ambush Sedd and his force in turn before they could complete a [[Chaos|dark]] [[Daemon Prince|ritual]].{{Fn|1}}

As Kurtha Sedd lay dead before them, however, Thiel realised that Rowd's rad-suit had been punctured in their initial escape and so he had been exposed to lethal levels of radiation while they were on the surface. Rowd died shortly afterwards.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Censure (Short Story)]] — [[Legacies of Betrayal (Anthology)]]

