Rykhel.wikitext:
{{SpaceMarinesPortal}}
{{Spoiler|source=Renegades (Short Story)}}
'''Rykhel''' was a [[Space Marine]] of the [[Avenging Sons]] [[Chapter]], a member of the [[3rd Company (Avenging Sons)|Third Company]].{{Fn|1}}


==History==
Rykhel served with the Third when the Company was sentenced to a penance patrol after the actions of their commanding officer, [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Gessart]], earned them censure from the Chapter's high command.  During their patrol, the Third were contacted by the [[Imperial]] government on the planet [[Helmabad]], who wanted assistance quelling a civil insurrection.  Unfortunately for the Avenging Sons, the rebels' strength had been vastly underestimated and by the time they arrived in-[[system]], the "small" uprising had turned into a civil war that had raged for eight years.  Nonetheless, the [[Space Marines]] engaged the rebel forces.{{Fn|1}}

Over the following seventy days, the Third Company was reduced to less than a third of their initial strength and had virtually run out of supplies.  They were also cut off from reinforcements by a shadow in the [[Warp]] that had fallen over the [[Helmabad system]].  After the Company's [[Librarian]], [[Zacherys]], sensed that the rebels were trying to open a [[warp rift]], Captain Gessart made the decision to abandon Helmabad, ultimately [[Renegade Space Marine|going renegade]] along with his loyal followers.  Rykhel initially did not protest as Gessart killed the Company's [[Chaplain]], [[Herdain]], along with any other [[Space Marines|Marine]] who resisted.  When the Company returned to their [[Strike Cruiser]], the ''[[Vengeful]]'', however, Rykhel escaped the ship by launching a [[saviour pod]] just as the renegades were about to translate into the Warp.{{Fn|1}}

Rykhel's pod was on course to return to Helmabad as the warp rift opened and the ''Vengeful'' escaped.{{Fn|1}}  Gessart believed that Rykhel had almost certainly died on Helmabad, although some of the renegades (in particular [[Heynke]]) thought that he may have survived.{{Fn|2}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Renegades (Short Story)]]
*{{Endn|2}}: [[The Rewards of Tolerance (Short Story)]]

