Ryvor.wikitext:
{{DarkAngelsPortal}}
'''Ryvor''' is a [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] in the [[Dark Angels]] [[Chapter]]'s [[Ravenwing]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
He was among its forces that [[Dark Angels Grand Master|Master]] [[Sammael]] led to aid [[Gehöft]] in late [[M41]]{{Fn|1}}. The [[Imperial]] world was the latest to be infected with [[Nurgle]]'s diseases, by the [[Blighted Claw]] [[Chaos Warband|Warband]] and their [[Plague Lord]] [[Paramyx]]. He was being targeted, however, by the [[White Scars]]' [[Master of the Hunt]] [[Kor'sarro Khan]], whose forces came to Gehöft to collect Paramyx's head. Sammael agreed to aid the Khan in this task and Ryvor was among those that accompanied the Ravenwing Master. Then as their [[Space Marine Company|Companies]] fought the Blighted Claw, Kor'sarro Khan and Sammael led their selected squadrons deep into the battlefield to hunt for the Plague Lord.{{Fn|2}} 

They soon found him deep in the battlefield, but before they attacked [[Paramyx]]{{Fn|2}}, [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] Ryvor spotted the battle flag of the [[Fallen Angel]] [[Skethon]]. The traitor was thought to have died after his last encounter with the [[Dark Angels]], but Skethon had survived and had allied his forces with the [[Blighted Claw]]. After Ryvor informed him of the Fallen Angel's flag, [[Dark Angels Grand Master|Master]] [[Sammael]] immediately ordered his [[Ravenwing]] squadrons to pursue the war machine the flag flew upon. Ryvor hesitantly brought up the [[White Scars]] and the aid the Ravenwing promised, but the Master simply gave him a knowing glance before leading the attack on Skethon. Abandoning their allies, however{{Fn|1}}, allowed [[Kor'sarro Khan]]'s squadron to be overrun by the Blighted Claw and only the [[Master of the Hunt]] escaped with his life. Paramyx was thus able to leave [[Gehöft]] and infect other [[Imperial]] worlds{{Fn|2}}, while Skethon managed to escape from the Ravenwing's grasp as well. The Dark Angels did, however, recover the Fallen Angel's personal journal and Sammael made ready to return it to his [[Chapter]]'s [[Inner Circle]]{{Fn|1}}. By then, though, Gehöft was doomed and the Ravenwing and other surviving Imperial forces, were evacuated before the world was destroyed by an [[Exterminatus]].{{Fn|2}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Sammael: Lord of the Eternal Hunt (Short Story)]]
*{{Endn|2}}: [[Kor'sarro Khan: Huntmaster (Short Story)]]

