Sa'kan.wikitext:
{{SalamandersPortal}}
'''Sa'kan''' is a [[Salamanders]] [[Primaris Space Marine]], part of squad Va'Lok in the [[3rd Company (Salamanders)|3rd Company]].{{Fn|3a}} 
==Biography==
[[Image:Sa'kan.jpg|thumb|right|180px|Sa'kan{{Fn|2}}]]
During the [[Pariah Crusade]] on [[Paradyce III]]{{Fn|1}} he was sent on a mission to make contact with Lieutenant [[Vorenus]] of the [[Ultramarines]] and find a way to unite their forces to retake the southern cities on the planet.{{Fn|3c}} When he first arrived to the planet his [[Thunderhawk]] crashed{{Fn|3a}}, killing the other [[Salamanders]] who came with him. After landing he was almost immediately attacked by members of the [[Death Korps of Krieg]] Who had been experimented on by [[Illuminor Szeras]]. After leaving the gunship he fought with several [[Necrons]] and found civilians who had managed to survive the battle in the city. Shortly after he encountered [[Sister]] [[Danica]], in the middle of a stand off with her over letting the civilians live or not they were attacked by a [[Deathmark]].{{Fn|3b}} After escaping the [[Deathmark]] they made their way to city core. Just as he told the civilians to head west they were ambushed by a [[Skorpekh Destroyer]] which cut off his right hand. Shortly after defeating it the [[Deathmark]] from before caught up with them, it killed [[Sister]] [[Danica]] and was then heavily damaged by Sa'kan before retreating, Sa'kan then told the civilians to go west again before leaving them. Later he found and killed the [[Deathmark]] as it was talking to [[Illuminor Szeras]], he then talked briefly with [[Szeras]] before moving on.{{Fn|3c}}

Later in the invasion, Sa'kan aided the [[Ultramarines]] [[Primaris Apothecary]] [[Brutus (Apothecary)|Brutus]] in recovering the [[Gene-seed]] of slain Ultramarines.{{Fn|2}} In the course of doing so, they discovered that some of the bodies of Brutus' [[Battle Brothers]] had gone missing and later learned they were being experimented upon by the Necrons.{{Fn|1}}
==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
''Sa'kan'' appears in the animated series [[Pariah Nexus (Animated Series)]] and [[The Tithes (Animated Series)]].{{Fn|1}}

