Sabraham.wikitext:
{{BloodAngelsPortal}}
[[Image:BAHeresy.jpg|thumb|right|275px|Sabraham{{Fn|1}}]]
'''Sabraham''' was a [[Legionary]] of the [[Blood Angels]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]], belonging to the [[121st Company (Blood Angels Legion)|121st Company]] during the [[Great Crusade]] and [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1}} 

==History==
Legionary Sabraham was a member of a Legion [[Tactical Squad]] at the time the Blood Angels were ordered to muster at the [[Nartaba System]] in preparation for the campaign in the [[Signus Cluster]], but he and his company never deployed to that operation. When the company's vessels were cast upon the tides of the [[Warp]], its members were spread across the small flotilla, each sub-unit believing for a time that it would meet its end upon the raging tides of unreality, until finally translating to a pocket of comparative calm coreward of the [[Maelstrom]]. Sabraham was present at the [[Conclave of Optera]] and survived the [[Alpha Legion]]'s ambush to fight in [[Pale Stars campaign (Horus Heresy)|subsequent battles]] in the region.{{Fn|1}}  

During the [[Raid on Kyro IV]], he was deployed alongside his squad into the depths of the mines of [[Kyro IV]], where he is thought to have fallen in combat when his squad was overwhelmed by a savage tide of the eyeless [[abhuman]] slaves who worked the mines, who were likely turned into living weapons by the machinations of the Alpha Legion.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[The Horus Heresy Book Six - Retribution]], pg. 99

