'''Sanian''' was a [[Hagia]]n [[esholi]] (a scholar, in the Hagian dialect of [[Low Gothic]]) who lived during the [[Sabbat Worlds Crusade]].{{Fn|1a}}


==Biography==
Sanian was born and raised in the town of [[Bhavnager]], before becoming an esholi leaving to find her "way" (Hagians putting great stock on one's personal destiny).{{Fn|1c}}

She was present in [[Holy Doctrinopolis|Hagia's capital city]] at the time of the Crusade's actions on Hagia.{{Fn|1a}} When [[Lord General]] [[Lugo]] gave the order to evacuate Hagia in the face of incoming [[Chaos]] reinforcements, a number of [[Imperial Guardsmen]] who had been experiencing visions of [[Saint Sabbat]] decided to disobey orders to join the evac fleet and instead travel to the [[Shrinehold of Saint Sabbat]], where the Saint's remains were interred. [[Trooper]] [[Brin Milo]] of the [[Tanith First and Only]] asked Sanian to accompany them as a guide, hoping to use her knowledge of [[Tembarong Road|the local area]] to reach the Shrinehold more quickly, and she agreed to travel with them.{{Fn|1b}}

