{{otheruses|USE=tech-priest|OTHERUSE=[[Chaos Space Marine]]|OTHERPAGE=Scaevolla}}
{{QuoteBox
|quote = ''"[[[Error]]] Damn not found."''<br>'''- Scaevola comments on potentially high [[Skitarii]] losses while<br> pursuing potential [[archeotech]] in the [[Necron]] tombs of Silva Tenebris'''{{Fn|1a}}
|}}
{{AdeptusMechanicusPortal}}
[[Image:Scaevola.jpg|thumb|right|220px|Scaevola]]
'''Scaevola''' is a [[Acquisitor (Adeptus Mechanicus)|Tech-Acquisitor]] hailing from [[Stygies VIII]]. As a tech-acquisitor her statement of purpose is ''To perceive the grander picture, to strive to acquire and understand for the benefit of all Mankind''.{{Fn|1}} She has harvested technology from a hundred [[xeno]]s races and delved into secrets unknown to even the [[Necron]]s.{{Fn|4}}


==Silva Tenebris==
Scaevola was part of the triumvirate commanding the [[Ark Mechanicus]] ship, the ''[[Caestus Metalican]]'' and advisor to [[Magos Dominus]] [[Faustinius]] during this mission. It is currently on a salvage mission to the newly rediscovered world of [[Silva Tenebris]]. The Ark Mechanicus is commanded by a triumvirate of tech-priests, with Magos Dominus Faustinius of [[Mars]] leading their mission. Tech-Acquisitor Scaevola is one of the supporting members of the triumvirate, alongside [[Lector-Dogmatis]] [[Videx]] of [[Metalica]].{{Fn|1}}{{Fn|2a}}


Her curiosity of [[Xenos]] tech upon the [[Necron]] [[Tomb World]] often puts her at odds with the puritanical Lector-Dogmatix [[Videx]] of [[Metalica]], who is also in service to Faustinius upon this mission. Scaevola sees this mission as a wondrous opportunity to discover tech secrets, gathering this knowledge for Mars and the good of all.{{Fn|1}}

Scaevola is secretly a [[Xenarite]] and encourages [[Faustinius]] to plunder the vaults of their Necron technology and knowledge. As a xenarite, Scaevola seeks to use xenos-tech in order to benefit humanity. Plundering these pristine xenos artefacts would surely increase her position amongst the Xenarites' hierarchy, as well as increase [[Stygies VIII]]'s power.{{Fn|1}} Unlike the [[heretek]] stowaway and fellow Xenarite, [[Epsilus Dammek-Yoth]], Scaevola doesn't seek to have alien technology define humanity, or to entirely replace humanity's biological forms with [[living metal]] bodies as Epsilus seeks to do.{{Fn|3a}}

Scaevola is excited when encountering [[Necron Destroyer]]s, stating that [[anti-grav|anti-gravitational]] technology is an area Stygies VIII's Magi have requested as high priority.{{Fn|1}}

==Trivia==
{{trivia}}
{{spoiler|source=Warhammer 40,000: Mechanicus}}
*Of the 4 possible endings of ''Warhammer 40,000: Mechanicus'', the Xenarite ending features Scaevola's mission to raid the Tomb World's library. Once successful, she gathers as much data from the [[Tomb World]] of [[Silva Tenebris]] as her internal data-stores can carry. Scaevola would subsequently head to Mars, babbling that she must report her findings to "The Dragon". This is likely a reference to the [[Dragon of Mars]], of which Faustinius is seemingly unaware, commenting that he assumes this "Dragon" is probably the title of some Xenarite leader.{{Fn|1b}} In the sequel game Mechanicus II, this proves to not be the canon ending.{{Fn|4}}

