The '''{{PAGENAME}}''' was the name given to one of the eight individuals which made up the mysterious [[Hand of Abaddon]], an organization within the [[Black Legion]] dedicated to reconstituting the [[Anathame]].{{Fn|1a}}

The only other [[Chaos Space Marine]] on the Hand besides the [[Butcher King]], the Scion of Plagues was a hulking putrid devotee of [[Nurgle]] armed with a massive axe and scythe. He was a member of the one of the old [[Traitor Legion]]s, though it is never stated which (though [[Death Guard]] is the most likely). He was also the most recent addition of the Hand, and was least effected by its constant infighting.{{Fn|1b}}

During the [[Battle of the Stygius Gilt]], the Scion of Plagues and his army of [[Plague Marine]]s and Nurgle abominations confronted the Imperial forces boarding the [[Blackstone Fortress]] the Hand used as their base. His forces reaped heavy losses on the Imperials and seemed poised for victory under the [[Mordian Iron Guard]] [[Sergeant]] [[Magda Kesh]] miraculously ascended to a [[Living Saint]] and incinerated the Chaos Space Marine with holy light.{{Fn|1e}}

