'''Segas''' was the first [[Chaplain]] of the [[Scythes of the Emperor]] [[Chapter]] of [[Space Marines]].{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
Segas was a [[Chaplain]] of the [[Ultramarines]] [[2nd Company (Ultramarines)|Second Company]] at the time of the [[Third Founding]]. Seeking to remove evidence of both [[Imperium Secundus]] and Guilliman's defiance of his own ''[[Codex Astartes]]'' by maintaining a phantom 11th Company, [[Chapter Master]] [[Tigris Decon]] sent Segas and [[Wenlocke]] to Sotha to offer [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Oberdeii]], the last surviving member of the Aegida Company, a choice of reassignment to the [[5th Company (Ultramarines)|5th Company]] or continuing to guard the Pharos as Master of a new 'Aegida Chapter'.{{Fn|2}}

Oberdeii, initially appalled that [[Rogal Dorn]] had initiated another founding, reluctantly agreed to found a new Chapter, but chose to name them the [[Scythes of the Emperor]]. Segas and Wenlocke joined the new Chapter, along with 72 veterans of the [[Orlan Conquest]].{{Fn|2}}

Segas was a noted scholar of Chapter lore, being well versed in the writings of [[Eikos Lamiad|Lamiad]], [[Lucretius Corvo|Corvo]] and [[Titus Prayto|Prayto]], amongst others.{{Fn|2}}

After his death, Segas's remains were interred on the reliquary world of [[Egottha]].{{Fn|1}}

