Selene (Sister Repentia).wikitext:
{{AdeptaSororitasPortal}}
'''Selene''' is a [[Sister Repentia]] of the [[Order of Our Martyred Lady]], who once held the rank of [[Canoness]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
{{Spoiler|source=Sisters of Battle (Comic Series)}}
However she took the [[Sister Repentia|Oath of the Penitent]], after the mission she led on [[Balta]] ended in disaster. It began, when Selene and 9 [[Sisters of Battle|Sisters]] she commanded, entered a cave to reclaim a relic from the world. However, while the man who gave the information to the [[Canoness]] claimed they would face no danger in doing so, the Sisters were soon ambushed. Arrayed against them were a large number of [[Cultist]]s and [[Daemon]]s of [[Nurgle]], and seeing them caused Selene to falter. Though it was only for a moment, it was enough for the forces of Nurgle to swarm the Sisters. As they fought, [[Sister Superior]] [[Veridyan]] and [[Battle Sister]] [[Cassia]] raced the relic to the Sisters' shuttle for safekeeping. They then returned to the others, but found them all dead, except for Selene who had been badly wounded.{{Fn|1}} 

The [[Canoness]] blamed herself for the [[Sisters of Battle|Sisters]]' deaths and told the two to escape and leave her to die with the fallen Sisters. [[Veridyan]] refused, though, and told Selene that her life was not hers to forfeit. The Canoness agreed, but said she would seek the [[Emperor]]'s forgiveness for her failings, by taking the [[Sister Repentia|Oath of the Penitent]]. Just after saying so, another group of [[Cultists]] and [[Daemons]] attacked them. Despite being heavily outnumbered, though, the Sisters fought together and succeeded in escaping from [[Balta]] with the relic. Afterwards, Selene would give a report about what happened and took full responsibility for her Sisters' deaths. She claimed she had been too trusting of the man, who had given her the relic's location. Selene had believed him that they would face no danger and this had lulled her into a false sense of safety. Her mistake in judgement would have killed them all, had it not been for Veridyan and [[Cassia]]. Their actions, and theirs alone, had allowed them to escape with the relic and their lives. Selene concluded, by stating that because of her failures on Balta, she no longer considered herself a Canoness or a Sister of Battle. Instead Selene once again took the Oath of the Penitent and became a [[Sister Repentia]]. Selene could only pray that by doing so, she would earn absolution for her failings - either in life or in death.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Sisters of Battle (Comic)]], Issue 3  

