Selgar Dorgaddon.wikitext:
{{SonsOfHorusPortal}}
'''Selgar Dorgaddon''' was [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] of the [[Sons of Horus]]' [[10th Company (Sons of Horus)|10th Company]] during the [[Siege of Terra]].{{Fn|1}}

==History==
By the end of the [[Great Crusade]], Dorgaddon was a regular [[Battle Brother]] in the [[10th Company (Sons of Horus)|10th Company]]. According to [[Euphrati Keeler]], he was of kind disposition at the time. Unlike his superior [[Garviel Loken]], Dorgaddon sided with the Traitors during the [[Battle of Isstvan III]];{{Fn|2a}} he subsequently rose in the ranks of the legion. In the process, he became increasingly cruel and monstrous, through a fragment of his original personality seemed to still cling to him like a ghost.{{Fn|2a}}{{Fn|2b}}

Commanding the 10th Company, by the final stages of the [[Siege of Terra|Siege]] Dorgaddon had fully committed himself to the madness of [[Chaos]] and was ignoring [[Abaddon]]'s orders.{{Fn|1}} He eventually encountered Euphrati Keeler and her column of refugees, recognising the former [[remembrancer]] from her time with the Captain's [[Traitor Legion|Legion]].{{Fn|2a}} This was not enough to stay his hand, and Dorgaddon gave the order to attack the refugees and then prepared to execute Keeler. However he was brutally killed by the [[Emperor's Champion]] [[Sigismund]] before his Company could land a single blow{{Fn|2b}} and the 10th was destroyed by Sigismund's own [[Sigismund's Seconds|forces]], shortly afterwards.{{Fn|2c}}

