Seoci.wikitext:
{{EldarPortal}}
'''Seoci''' was an [[Eldar]] of [[Craftworld]] [[Lugganath]].{{Fn|1}}

Seoci walked many [[Eldar Path|paths]] over the course of his life.  Notably, he was almost trapped on the Path of the Poet after spending too long on that path.  He was rescued from that fate by [[Ailios]], becoming lovers as a result, but as a side-effect of almost being trapped, he would occasionally compose poems without meaning to.{{Fn|1}}

During his time with Ailios, he referred to her as ''sorrowrose'', while she, in turn, called him ''water len''.{{Fn|1}}

Following this, Soeci and Ailios walked the Paths together, eventually ending up on the Path of the Seer.  After a battle which cost many eldar, however, Ailios became trapped on that path, unable to join Seoci as he moved on to the Path of the Hunter.  Seoci joined the [[Searing Zephyrs]], becoming a [[Crimson Hunter]] [[Aspect Warrior]].{{Fn|1}}

In Seoci's last mission as a Crimson Hunter, the forces of Lugganath, along with their [[Eldar Corsair|corsair]] allies, attempted to assassinate the [[Ork]] [[Big Mek]] known as [[Gorkog Chrometeef]], as their seers predicted that allowing Chrometeef to live would result in the eventual destruction of their Craftworld to an [[Imperium|Imperial]] [[Crusade]].  Seoci decided that he was going to leave the Path of the Hunter after the mission after witnessing the single-minded battlelust of his [[Exarch]], [[Liosa]].  However, as the Eldar attacked the Orks, Chrometeef launched his new flagship, which the Eldar named ''[[Beastmother]]''.{{Fn|1}}

Seoci was able to rally the remaining Eldar pilots; together they disabled a number of the craft's power generators and take out its anti-grav units.  This caused the ''Beastmother'' to crash-land, killing Chrometeef and completing the mission.  Seoci, however, was killed in the flight to escape the crashing ship.{{Fn|1}}

As Seoci lay dying, he was able to remove his [[War Mask]], before predicting that, in death, he would be called back into service as a [[Hemlock Wraithfighter|wraithfighter]].  His [[spirit stone]] was recovered after the battle.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Wraithbound (Short Story)]] - [[On Wings of Blood (Anthology)]]

