Seriadne Hekht.wikitext:
{{ChaosPortal}}
'''Seriadne Hekht''' is the [[Traitor General (Traitor Guard)|Traitor General]] of the [[Styxx 777th Warwolves]], a [[Traitor Guard]] [[Regiment]].{{Fn|1b}}

==History==
Like all of the [[Styxx 777th]], Hekht was once loyal to the [[Imperium]]{{Fn|1b}}, until the unit was sent to reinforce the [[Imperial]] world [[Moroch (Frontier World)|Moroch]] in [[M42]]. This was as the [[Imperium]] was [[Sanctus Wall|preparing]] for [[Abaddon the Despoiler]]'s hordes, as they [[Nachmund Rift War|bore down]] upon Moroch and the other worlds of the [[Gorandahl Sub-sector]]. The [[Black Legion]] became aware of this, however, and its [[Sorcerers]] determined which [[Regiments]] would be sent to reinforce the [[Sub-sector]]. This information was then given to the [[Alpha Legion]], whose [[Human]] agents infiltrated the targeted Regiments and began corrupting them to serve the Black Legion. The Styxx and other Regiments being sent to Moroch were infiltrated and successfully rotted from the inside out.{{Fn|1a}} 

When [[Moroch (Frontier World)|Moroch]]'s reinforcements finally reached the world, they had all been fully corrupted by the [[Alpha Legion]] and were now loyal to the [[Black Legion]]{{Fn|1a}}. Hekht herself became the [[Styxx 777th]]'s [[Traitor General (Traitor Guard)|Traitor General]] and days after arriving on Moroch, she led them in attacking the world beside the other newly arrived Traitor Guard. They sought to overthrow the Imperium's rule on Moroch, which would greatly aid the Black Legion when its hordes [[Nachmund Rift War|invaded]] the [[Gorandahl Sub-sector]]. With the element of surprise on their side, the Traitor Guard soon surrounded Moroch's capital '''Magnificentia'''{{Fn|1a}}. However a single [[Phobos Strike Team]], led by [[Vanguard Infiltrator#Types of Vanguard Infiltrators|Infiltrator Sergeant]] [[Justarian]], was sent to aid the besieged world. The [[Vanguard Space Marine]]s then began attacking the world's outposts, that were held by the Traitor Guard. The attacks soon forced the [[Regiment]]'s Traitor Generals to respond, by sending [[Blooded Kill Team]]s to wipe out Justarian's Strike Team. These would be led by their [[Traitor Lieutenant]]s, but caution was needed in selecting them. For any success in destroying the Vanguard Space Marines, could garner the Lieutenant enough favor from the [[Chaos Gods]] to challenge the General for their position. Among those selected by Hekht was the [[Traitor Commissar]] [[Igmus Lothar]]. This was due to his zealously and, Hekht hoped, loyalty to her.{{Fn|1b}} 

==Sources==
