'''{{PAGENAME}}''' was the [[Space Marine Captain|Battle-Captain]] of the [[Blood Angels]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legion's]] [[121st Company (Blood Angels Legion)|121st Company]] during the [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1}}

His company missed the muster for the [[Signus Cluster]] campaign after being caught in a [[warp storm]], emerging days later on the edge of the [[Maelstrom]] to find that four years had passed in realspace. Serron came to [[Optera IV]] when his fleet detected [[Nathaniel Garro]]'s [[astropath]]ic summons, learning that [[Sanguinius]] and the Blood Angels were believed to have been lost save for the honour guard on [[Baal]]. Grieving for his [[primarch]], Serron refused to return to [[Terra]] with Garro, stating that his company would seek out the enemy wherever they were to be found. After the [[Alpha Legion]] ambushed the conclave, Serron and his company threw themselves into [[Pale Stars campaign (Horus Heresy)|the war across]] [[the Pale Stars]], heedless of their own lives. They clashed with the Alpha Legion in the mines of [[Kyro IV]], on the inner moons of [[771/58]], and through the [[xenos]]-haunted mire-seas of [[Sidaiva]] before suddenly disengaging from the enemy at [[Psiom Zeta-1]] to make a [[warp]]-jump in the direction of [[Segmentum Solar]]. Some of the 121st Company are believed to have been present at the [[Siege of Terra]].{{fn|1}}

