Setekh (Giant Necron).wikitext:
{{NecronsPortal}}
{{otheruses|USE=giant [[Necron]]|OTHERUSE=Necron [[Nemesor]]|OTHERPAGE=Setekh (Nemesor)}}
[[Image:Kal_Jericho_Seketh_1.png|thumb|right|250px|The Setekh confronting an inquisitorial retenue{{Fn|1}}.]]
'''Setekh''' is the name of a powerful giant [[Necron]] that was created long ago during the [[War in Heaven (Necron)|War in Heaven]].

== History ==
Crafted as one of the greatest creations of the [[Necrontyr]], it quickly became one of the most powerful servants of the [[C'tan]].  During ancient times, its purpose was to bring death to every corner of the galaxy whilst raising black pyramidical monuments to honour its deathless masters.  Such acts were conducted on a thousand blasted and ruined worlds.  For reasons unknown, it became trapped within its hibernation sarcophagus and became lost onboard the [[Space Hulk]] ''[[Kronos (Space Hulk)|Kronos]]'' where it drifted in its sleep for sixty million years.{{Fn|1}}

During the [[Age of the Imperium]], [[Inquisitor]] [[Jena Orechiel]] led her retinue (including her son, [[Kal Jerico]]) to deprive the awakening [[C'tan]] of the Setekh.  The ancient creation had awoken and had forgotten its great purpose but recognized that invaders had intruded upon its sanctuary thus leading to it taking its wrath against them.  After awakening, it had only tapped into a fraction of its power whilst drawing power from its sarcophagus, where it effortlessly killed the [[Ordo Xenos]] retinue and members of the [[Deathwatch]] with powerful energy blasts.  [[Cyclonic torpedo]]s were later deployed against the Space Hulk where it was believed that the Setekh was either destroyed by being blasted into the [[warp]] or sufficiently damaged that it became useless to its C'tan masters.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Kal Jerico (Graphic Novel Series)]] ''"Above and Beyond"'' Parts 6-9

[[Category:Characters (Necrons)]]

Setekh (Nemesor).wikitext:
{{ambig|subject=Necron Nemesor|disambiguation=Setekh}}
{{NecronsPortal}}
'''Setekh''' was the name of a cunning [[Necron]] [[Nemesor]] that excelled in propaganda, espionage, and the manipulation of psychological weakness.{{Fn|1a}}

==Biography==
Setekh was born into elite echelon of nobility. He had attended one of the [[Necrontyr]]'s most celebrated military academies, where he met [[Nemesor]] [[Zahndrekh]], his rival and confidant. After winning his commission, he was given an army and sent off to fight separatists in [[Yama]] during the [[Wars of Secession]].{{Fn|1a}}

He later worked under [[Imotekh|Imotekh the Stormlord]] as a privateer of sorts. In exchange for freedom to operate, and as penance for undisclosed sins, he had agreed to sacrifice his tomb world, and have it marked as lost to a supernova during the great sleep. Since then, his small dynasty had been nomadic, based entirely aboard his fleet, and charged with furthering the interests of the [[Sautekh Dynasty]] among the [[Ghoul Stars]].{{Fn|1b}}

Setekh failed to convince [[Obyron|Varguard Obyron]] to betray his master. He fought them both in [[Doahht]]'s core, where the Varguard shoved his face towards the planet's unstable engine, burning the Nemesor's face until it remained black and melted.{{Fn|1c}}

==Wargear==
In battle, Setekh wields a [[Staff of Light]] identical to [[Nemesor]] [[Zahndrekh]]'s, save for the blue light blazing from its power core, in contrast to Zahndrekh’s green. He also relies on his twin [[Canoptek Skolopendra|canoptek skolopendra]] hunting beasts, [[Sepa and Sata|''Sepa'' and ''Sata'']].{{Fn|1a}}

