Seumas.wikitext:
{{DeathwatchPortal}}
'''Seumas''' was a [[Watch Captain]] of the [[Deathwatch]].{{Fn|1}}

At one point, Seumas (along with his fellow Watch Captains [[Drusus (Deathwatch)|Drusus]] and [[Bresnik]]) were called on to consider a petition by [[Chaplain]] [[Ortan Cassius]] to lead a [[Kill-Team]] to the [[Ghosarian System]], in order to discover the fate of a [[Kill Team Excis|previous team]] who had failed to report in. After hearing Cassius's report on the events leading up to the mission, both Drusus and Bresnik denied Cassius's request, believing a mere delayed report was insufficient to justify a priority mission when the Deathwatch's resources were already spread thin. Seumas, however, believed that Cassius's report supported [[Cult of the Four-Armed Emperor|a pattern]] that Seumas had noticed on a number of Imperial worlds. After the council, Seumas talked with Cassius privately, helping him to go around the Watch Captains' backs, contact [[Watch Commander]] [[Quovis Vaerion]] and organise a mission anyway.{{Fn|1}}

==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
===Notes===
Seumas's Chapter of origin is not explicitly stated in the source; however, his Chapter's symbol is stated to be a black, winged lightning bolt on a yellow field, possibly making him a member of the [[Marines Malevolent]].

