Shadowlord (Archon).wikitext:
{{DrukhariPortal}}
{{Fanatic}}
The '''Shadowlord'''{{Fn|2}} is a [[Drukhari]] [[Archon]].{{Fn|1b}} 
==History==
He was part{{Fn|1b}} of an alliance with [[Chaos]] and [[Ork]] forces, that [[Dark Crusade (Charydis Sector)|invaded]] the [[Imperium]]'s [[Charydis Sector]], in late [[M41]]. One of the battles fought in the invasion, was on an Imperial world that contained an inactive [[Warlord Titan]]. This Titan was coveted by [[Abaddon the Despoiler]], who personally commanded the [[Black Legion]]'s forces in the alliance, and he used his [[Xenos]] allies to aid him in its capture.{{Fn|1a}} Arrayed against them, however, was the [[Astra Militarum]] and the [[Dark Angels]] [[Chapter]], who were led by [[Dark Angels Supreme Grand Master|Grand Master]] [[Azrael]]. The Imperial forces were also being aided by the [[Craftworld]]s [[Miel Carn]] and [[Saim-Hann]], who had agreed to aid in the Charydis Sector's defense.{{Fn|2}} Under Abaddon's orders though, the Shadowlord and Orks lured Azrael away from the spaceport that held the Warlord Titan. Once they did so, the Black Legion launched its attempt to secure the Titan.{{Fn|1a}} 

Afterwards, the [[Archon]] personally led his forces against the [[Craftworld]] [[Miel Carn]] and inflicted severe causalities against them. This caused the Craftworld's forces to flee and they likely would have been routed, if Miel Carn's [[Avatar of Khaine]] and [[Fire Dragon]]s had not barred the Shadowlord's path. Even so, the [[Archon]] was able to deal several wounds to the Avatar. As the battle wore on, the [[Black Legion]] eventually managed to secure the [[Warlord Titan]]. Its loss, led the surviving Imperial and [[Craftworld]] forces to flee from the world.{{Fn|2}}
==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
The ''Shadowlord''{{Fn|2}} was created by '''Michael Andreson''' and he appeared in the [[The Citadel Journal 46]]{{Fn|1b}} and [[The Citadel Journal 47]].{{Fn|2}}

