Sharsi.wikitext:
{{EldarPortal}}
'''Sharsi, Keeper of the Wandering Cohort''', is a brightly robed [[Asuryani]] [[Farseer]], who steals rare artifacts. Some of which, were taken from the [[Imperium]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
The [[Farseer]] was among{{Fn|1}} the [[Asuryani]] forces, that invaded the [[Chinchare sub-sector]], in the wake of the [[13th Black Crusade]]. However the [[Imperium]] later launched the [[Dark Crusade (Imperium)|Dark Crusade]]'s [[Kith Campaign]] against the invading [[Xenos]]{{Fn|2}} and Sharsi would become one of its priority targets. He was known to the Imperium, as the [[Farseer]] had been active in several nearby [[Sectors]], and was considered a frail and cowardly creature, who resorted to attacking its forces from behind. Due to his past thefts, the Imperium's forces in the Kith Campaign were urged to kill the Farseer at all costs, before he struck at any of its undefended worlds. However, while the Asuryani were eventually defeated by the Imperium, Sharsi survived the conflict.{{Fn|1}}
==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
''Sharsi'' was created for the [[Dark Crusade Campaign]], by the '''Hobby Center''' staff of [[Games Workshop]]'s '''Buckland Hills''' store{{Fn|1}} in '''Manchester, Connecticut, USA'''.{{Fn|3}}

