Shk'xil.wikitext:
{{SlaaneshPortal}}
'''Shk'xil''' is a [[Slaanesh]] [[Keeper of Secrets]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
In [[M42]], it was among the [[Daemons]] of [[Slaanesh]] who invaded the [[Imperial]] world [[Persiphon]]. This was after a civil war broke out between the world's six '''Halls of Excellence''', which competed against each other to be judged the best at training the world's highly rated [[Guardsmen]]. The need to achieve victory, later led each of the Halls' war clerics to appeal to [[Chaos|dark powers]] and caused [[Slaanesh]]'s Daemons to invade Persiphon. Shk'xil and five other [[Keepers of Secrets|Keepers]] would join the attack and laid claim to the world. The influence of the Keepers of Secrets enveloped Persiphon and caused the veil between the [[warp]] and [[realspace]] to weaken further. As a result, nightmarish transformations had swept across the world and each Keeper ruled a unique realm, from the now corrupted Halls of Excellence. The entire '''Walast Province''' was ruled by Shk'xil and was transformed through warp sorcery into a colossal amphitheatre ringed by jagged yet elegant mountains. Here, mortal and Daemonic champions alike stalked one another through the shattered ruins of homes and shrines, seeking to slay their rivals and in doing so they would earn Shk'xil's adoration. Though an [[Ultramarines]] strike force, led by [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Aurus (Captain)|Aurus]], has now come to Persiphon' aid, the [[Space Marines]] are heavily outnumbered by Slaanesh's Daemons and the world's corrupted population. This has led [[Inquisitor]] [[Rudran Luc]] to call upon the [[Grey Knights]] for aid in saving Persiphon.{{Fn|1}} 

==Sources==
