Silberlant Sevos.wikitext:
{{NecromundaPortal}}
'''Silberlant Sevos''', also known as ''The Whisperer'', ''The Ghost of primus'', or ''The Infotek'' {{Fn|1a}} is a [[Whisper Merchant]] exile from [[House Van Saar]] on [[Necromunda (planet)|Necromunda]].{{Fn|1d}}
[[File:SevosInfotek.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Silberlant Sevos{{Fn|1d}}]]
==Biography==
Silberlant Sevos attempted to merge his mind with the sacred [[STC]] through a synaptic-inload interface, but the STC rejected him, leaving him physically and mentally broken. [[House Van Saar]] disowned him, casting his remains into the [[underhive]] and erasing his name from their records for violating their laws.{{Fn|1d}}

As he lay dying, he discovered he could perceive and interact with the hive's electronic systems. He took control of a group of maintenance [[servitor]]s, which carried him to safety and provided nourishment. Over time, he seized control of more hive systems and used stolen technology to construct a suspensor chair that could transport and protect his weakened body.{{Fn|1d}}

Sevos could also steal data secrets transmitted through the city's electro highways. Erasing his past, he became a [[Whisper Merchant]], amassing wealth through information trade. Foreseeing the chaos of the [[Great Darkness]], he took refuge in the underhive, continuing to manipulate events from the shadows.{{Fn|1d}}

==The Credo Rebellion==
{{Spoiler|source=The Aranthian Succession - Ruins of Jardlan}}
While the world was caught up in the [[Prophet of Redemption]]'s crusade to [[Temenos]], Sevos decoded [[Lady Credo]]'s vox transmissions to her agents and discovered clues about the true power behind the pilgrimage. He realized the threat posed by [[Ozostium]] and a returned [[House Aranthus]] to Necromunda, which could jeopardize his chances of being welcomed back into his clan if the social order collapsed. Though Sevos had no love for [[House Helmawr]] or [[Lady Haera]], he valued the stability the Imperial House provided. He used Hive Primus' systems to delay Haera's enemies, ensured her aircraft was ready, and scrubbed logs to hide her flight.{{Fn|1a}}

Sevos intercepted vox transmissions between [[Sharkan]], leader of the [[Techrunners]], and loyal Van Saar agents in the [[Palatine Cluster]], pinpointing Haera's location near [[Echolus Alpha]]. Sevos sent misleading messages to Sharkan to divert the hunters away from Haera. Concurrently, he hacked into the Enforcer code-net and impersonated Provost-Marshal [[Logun Kane]] to send Haera a priority directive to head to [[Spoiltown]]. He also sent a corresponding message to Kane, manipulating both sides to ensure Haera's safety.{{Fn|1b}}

Sevos was eventually located by [[Lady Credo]]'s spies. He considered escape but knew it was unlikely given his pursuers' proximity. As he prepared to defend himself, [[Delaque]] agents joined him, offering their protection.{{Fn|1c}}

