Sin.wikitext:
{{ChaosPortal}}
{{spoiler|source=Gaunt's Ghosts (Novel Series)}}
[[Pater (Chaos)|Pater]] '''Sin''' was the leader of the [[Chaos Cult]] known as the [[Infardi]] on [[Hagia]] during the [[Sabbat Worlds Crusade]].{{Fn|1a}}


==Biography==
After the Infardi seized control of Hagia, a detachment of the Sabbat Crusade led by [[Lord General]] [[Lugo]]{{Fn|1b}} was despatched to retake the planet.{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1b}} During the Hagia campaign, Sin was present in Hagia's capital city, the [[Holy Doctrinopolis]].{{Fn|1b}}

Although the Imperials made good progress capturing the city, Sin's men were able to capture [[Colonel]] [[Colm Corbec]] of the [[Tanith First and Only]]. Sin forced Corbec to watch as his fellow captive, [[Trooper]] [[Yael (Tanith)|Yael]], was tortured to death in front of him, through a parody of the [[Nine Holy Wounds]] inflicted on [[Saint Sabbat]].{{Fn|1b}}

Corbec was able to break free and meet up with a Tanith rescue squad led by [[Sergeant (Imperial Guard)|Sergeant]] [[Gol Kolea]]. Although Corbec and his rescuers killed a number of the Infardi that had taken the Colonel prisoner, Sin himself had managed to escape the city.{{Fn|1c}} Worse for the Imperials, Sin had set a trap in the desecrated shrine that was triggered by Guardsmen of the [[Brevian Centennials]] as they attempted to retake the Citadel.{{Fn|1c}}{{Fn|1d}} The trap not only destroyed the Citadel, killing many of the Brevians, but also acted as an [[astropathic]] beacon that signalled a nearby Chaos fleet. Lord General Lugo was forced to order the evacuation of the surviving Imperial forces on Hagia.{{Fn|1d}}

Corbec later avenged Yael by killing Sin on [[Herodor]].{{Cite This}}

==Appearance==
Sin was a tall, powerfully-built human, whose entire head was covered with tattoos depicting the [[Emperor of Mankind]] being tortured by [[daemon]]s, with Sin's right eye forming the Emperor's screaming mouth. His teeth were replaced with needle-sharp steel implants.{{Fn|1b}}

