'''Skethon''' is a [[Nurgle]]-worshiping [[Fallen Angel]], who has escaped the [[Dark Angels]]' attempts to capture him.{{Fn|1}}

==History==
He was thought dead after their last encounter, but Skethon survived and later allied himself{{Fn|1}} with the [[Plague Lord]] [[Paramyx]].{{Fn|2}} The [[Fallen Angel]]'s forces would then aid{{Fn|1}} the [[Blighted Claw]] [[Chaos Warband|Warband]] in invading [[Imperial]] worlds and infecting them with [[Nurgle]]'s diseases. One such world was [[Gehöft]] and the Imperium would come to its defence and to put an end to Paramyx's attacks. Among the Imperial forces were the [[White Scars]] led by the [[Master of the Hunt]] [[Kor'sarro Khan]], who had been tasked by his [[Chapter]] with killing the Blighted Claw's Plague Lord. The [[Dark Angels]]' [[Ravenwing]] also came to Gehöft's defense and its [[Dark Angels Grand Master|Master]], [[Sammael]], agreed to aid the Khan in his hunt. While their [[Space Marine Company|Companies]] fought to defend the world, they each led a squadron to find the Plague Lord as the battle raged around them. They succeeded in finding Paramyx, but before they reached him{{Fn|2}}, the Ravenwing spotted Skethon's battle flag on a nearby war engine.{{Fn|1}} 

Known as '''The Threefold Serpent''', Skethon's sigil depicted a serpent with three heads, tied in a knot on a dark green field. Upon seeing this, [[Sammael]] knew that the [[Fallen Angel]] still lived and ordered his squadron to pursue the war engine. Without the [[Ravenwing]]'s aid, however, [[Kor'sarro Khan]]'s squadron was overrun and only the [[Master of the Hunt]] was able to escape{{Fn|1}}. This allowed [[Paramyx]] to leave [[Gehöft]], to find another world to infect{{Fn|2}} and Sammael's squadron failed to capture a fleeing Skethon as well. The Ravenwing's [[Dark Angels Grand Master|Master]], however, had suspected from the start his efforts would not succeed, even as Sammael gave the order to abandon the Khan's squadron. He did manage to obtain a book, though, that was enshrined in a chapel within the war engine that bore Skethon's battle flag. Sammael thought it was the Fallen Angel's personal journal, which seemed to detail Skethor’s journeys since abandoning the [[Dark Angels]]. Sammael knew his duty was to return the journal to his [[Chapter]]'s [[Inner Circle]]{{Fn|1}} and, as Gehöft was now doomed to suffer [[Exterminatus]]{{Fn|2}}, the Ravenwing evacuated from the world.{{Fn|1}}

