Slyte.wikitext:
{{ChaosPortal}}
Slyte is a powerful [[daemon]], described as a "Daemonicus Arcana Majoris," which threatened destruction of the entire Imperium before being banished by [[Gideon Ravenor]].{{Fn|1}} It is unknown which of the [[Gods of Chaos]] Slyte is connect with, although its association with decay would suggest [[Nurgle]].{{Fn|2}}

== History ==
While Ravenor and his team were investigating [[flect]]s, his Interrogator [[Carl Thonius]] became addicted.{{Fn|3}}  One flect that Thonius used happened to contain Slyte, which immediately possessed him.{{Fn|2a}}  Thonius managed to suppress Slyte for the time being, but Slyte began to manifest when Thonius was in extreme danger to save his life.{{Fn|2b}} Attempting to foil [[Zygmunt Molotch]]'s schemes, Thonius was nearly killed and Slyte manifested. Slyte killed [[Jader Trice]], badly wounded Molotch, and destroyed their tome of [[Enuncia]]. However, [[Kara Swole]] witnessed the transformation and was horrified.{{Fn|2c}} Still in control, but being subtly manipulated by the daemon, Thonius healed [[Kara Swole]]'s terminal cancer but convinced her not to tell Ravenor about Slyte.{{Fn|2d}}

Ultimately, Thonius's mind was consumed and Slyte unleashed. Ravenor was only able to banish the daemon by allying with his mortal enemy Molotch and using an improvised Chaos ritual.{{Fn|1a}}

==Abilities==
Slyte initially manifested in Thonius's body. It could cause people or objects it touched to rapidly rot and decay. Slyte was also near-immune to Enuncia.{{Fn|2c}} It also had powerful healing abilities.{{Fn|2d}}

When it fully manifested, Slyte was a mountain-sized pillar of rotten tentacles tipped with fingers or mouths. Anything it touched rotted away.{{Fn|1b}}

