Solomon Lok.wikitext:
{{OrdoXenosPortal}}
[[Image:Soloman_Lok.jpg|thumb|right|210px|Inquisitor Lord Solomon Lok]] 
'''Solomon Lok''' was the [[Ordo Xenos]] [[Inquisitor]] charged with investigating the sudden loss of contact from a research facility on [[Beta Anphelion IV]] in 850.[[M41]].{{Fn|1}}


==Biography==
*{{main|Anphelion Project}}
Solomon Lok was a veteran of the [[Chinchare Hrud Infestation]].{{Fn|1}}

He, the [[Elysian Drop Troops 99th]] 'D' Detachment (led by [[Major]] [[Durra]]), a detachment of the [[Cadian 226th]], an [[Adeptus Mechanicus]] Biologis Exploritas force headed by [[Magos Biologis]] [[Arthon]] (seconded from [[forge world]] [[Gryphonne IV]]) and a task force of the [[Red Scorpions]] [[chapter]] (led by [[Carab Culln]]) went into orbit above the clouded moon. After a fierce battle on Beta Anphelion IV, the Red Scorpions received orders to evacuate themselves, and only themselves. The transport requisitioned for the mission refused all of Lok's requests, stranding Lok and the small force of survivors on the moon as the Tyranids closed in. In the last battle, Lok succeeded in taking down a [[Hierophant]] [[bio-titan]], only to see two more stride out of the ammonia fog. Lok died, betrayed by his superiors and his faith.{{Fn|1}}

==Retinue==
Lok's [[Inquisitorial Retinue|retinue]] consisted of [[Autosavant]] [[Wassily]], who kept a log of the Anphelion incident to the end, [[Astropath]] [[Zarneck]], who transmitted the log to Lord [[Varius (Inquisitor)|Varius]] (Lok's superior), a [[servo skull]], and [[Major]] [[Durra]], [[Detachment D-99]].{{Fn|1}}

